// A `std.log` attribute value must be a scalar — the `*_with` map's value type is
// `string | int | float | bool`. A non-scalar value (here a `List<int>`) is a compile-time type
// error, caught as the map literal absorbs the expected union value type at the call site (not a
// runtime failure). Mirrors `std.tracing`'s `set_attribute` scalar-only rule.
// expect: error E0007 at 8:34
// expect: exit 1
use std.log
log.info_with("tagged", {"tags": [1, 2, 3]})
